# CashConvert — Privacy Policy

**Last updated: April 2026**

## Overview

CashConvert is a Chrome extension that shows live exchange rates and provides a world currency converter. This policy explains how the extension handles your data.

## Data collection

CashConvert does **not** collect, store, transmit or share any personal data with third parties.

## How it works

- Exchange rates are fetched from the Frankfurter API (https://api.frankfurter.app), which sources data from the European Central Bank
- Rates are cached locally in `chrome.storage.local` for up to 60 minutes to avoid unnecessary requests
- Your preferred base currency is saved locally in `chrome.storage.local` and never leaves your device
- No personal data is sent to any server — only a standard HTTPS request to api.frankfurter.app to retrieve public exchange rate data

## Permissions

| Permission | Reason |
|---|---|
| `storage` | To cache exchange rates and save your base currency preference |
| `sidePanel` | To display CashConvert as a browser side panel |

## Third party services

CashConvert fetches exchange rate data from **Frankfurter** (https://api.frankfurter.app), a free public API that provides European Central Bank exchange rates. No personal data is sent in these requests — they are standard HTTPS GET requests for publicly available rate data.

